 ## Overview
-Fractal compression is a lossy volume compression method that exploits self-similarity within the dataset by mapping each "range block" to a larger, dissimilar "domain block" from the same volume, storing only the affine transformation required to convert the domain block into the range block [S1]. Unlike vector quantization, which stores a reference to a codeword, fractal compression stores the geometric relationship between two different-sized blocks, allowing for high compression ratios at the cost of extreme encoding complexity and iterative reconstruction during decoding [S1].
+Fractal compression is a lossy volume compression method that exploits self-similarity within the dataset by mapping each "range block" to a larger, most similar "domain block" from the same volume, storing only the affine transformation required to convert the domain block into the range block [S1]. Unlike vector quantization, which stores a reference to a codeword, fractal compression stores the geometric relationship between two different-sized blocks, allowing for high compression ratios at the cost of extreme encoding complexity and iterative reconstruction during decoding [S1].
 
